1
00:00:00,150 --> 00:00:20,817
Midnight City had built a throne at the airport. I thought that was
considerate as hell until a nigga in a silver cape told me it wasn't
mine. "It's for the victor of the tournament." "Nigga, then why you
making me walk past it?" "You have not won." "You have not seen me
lose. We both working with expectations.

2
00:00:21,067 --> 00:00:45,658
Move the chair." A guard behind him lowered his eyes. "That nigga
wants the throne brought over," another whispered. "That nigga just
landed." "Nigga, I been sitting all flight. I know what kind of chair
I deserve." The first guard nodded before he remembered whose rifle he
was carrying. He had a tall hat, a little mustache, and twenty men
behind him holding gold rifles.

3
00:00:45,909 --> 00:01:04,887
Every rifle turned toward me at the same time. Shawna stepped out of
the police Lamborghini, stretched after the flight, and took one look
at the situation. "Baby, we just landed." "I know. These niggas
already hiding my furniture." The silver cape made a noise in his
throat.

4
00:01:05,136 --> 00:01:25,519
Tank got out of the next car carrying a garment bag in one hand and
the expression he usually wore before putting somebody through a
closed door. Rosa was still in the car doing her lipstick. She rolled
down the window to see who was about to interrupt her vacation. "Is
that your king?" she asked the silver cape.

5
00:01:25,769 --> 00:01:42,924
"I am Lord Octavian Rusk, master of ceremonies." "Then do a ceremony
where you get out of the way." Behind us, the whole airport had
stopped pretending it was busy. Pilots watched from the stairs of
their jets. Baggage men stood on their carts.

6
00:01:43,174 --> 00:02:04,860
A woman in a white flight uniform took her sunglasses off slowly, like
her eyes deserved this without anything between them and me. I had
come to Midnight City because Emperor Zero thought the world was
something he could buy, and General Solomon Saint had died proving
that a nigga can have a whole army and still pick the wrong island.

7
00:02:05,110 --> 00:02:24,973
We had found enough money under Isla Gloria to make rich men look
poor. We had also found enough of Zero's secrets to make him want all
of us dead. He had sent an invitation anyway. Black card. Silver
letters. My name bigger than the address. COME AND CLAIM WHAT YOU
THINK YOU DESERVE.

8
00:02:25,223 --> 00:02:44,322
Shawna had read it twice, then asked if there would be dancing. That
was why I loved my wife. A man could threaten the future of everybody
we knew and this woman would still make sure I packed my good shoes.
The ship from Isla Gloria had taken us as far as the mainland port.

9
00:02:44,572 --> 00:03:04,638
We changed to planes there, cars loaded into cargo holds, because a
nigga was not arriving at a tournament of criminal kings in a rented
van. Isolde took a different flight from the same airfield. Vegas. She
wanted the room above Marcellus's workshop ready for dancing when he
came home.

10
00:03:04,888 --> 00:03:28,334
She kissed him at the gate, straightened his collar, and told him to
call before he started missing her dramatically. The old nigga called
from the next gate. Already? I asked. We lost thirty-five years to
poor timing. I'm improving. He held the phone out. Isolde told me to
bring him back with all his fingers because she needed somebody to
fasten her necklaces.

11
00:03:28,584 --> 00:03:47,726
Nigga, he heard you. I want you to hear me too. I promised. Marcellus
took his phone back and walked toward our plane smiling at it like
somebody had finally taught a jewel to speak. One of the airport
workers finally came close enough to stop pretending he was moving
luggage.

12
00:03:47,976 --> 00:04:12,946
Young nigga, twenty-seven maybe, blue uniform, white gloves, a whole
expression of recognition trying to get out through his mouth. "That's
the nigga," he whispered to another worker. "Which nigga?" "The island
nigga. The champion. The cop." "Those the same nigga?" I turned.
"Nigga, I heard all three descriptions." The first worker almost
dropped his clipboard. "Captain. I watched the championship.

13
00:04:13,196 --> 00:04:35,588
My father said no man could do all that." "Your father doing better
now?" He laughed so suddenly the second worker started laughing too.
"He owes me money." "Nigga, collect it with interest. I worked hard on
that argument." Shawna leaned against my shoulder, smiling. The worker
looked at her and forgot the clipboard completely. It hit the ground.

14
00:04:35,838 --> 00:05:01,644
His friend caught it off the bounce and bowed like that had been a
planned part of welcoming my wife. "Mrs. Aiden," he said. "Shawna,"
she told him. "Yes. Of course. Shawna. We watched you sing. My mother
made everybody be quiet. Even my father. Especially my father." "Your
mother sounds talented," my wife said. Nigga, both workers looked
blessed personally. Rusk tried to interrupt.

15
00:05:01,894 --> 00:05:20,262
Neither one heard him the first time. A king could stand on a whole
throne beside these niggas and still lose their attention to my wife
being nice for twelve seconds. The first worker took off his airport
badge. "Would you sign the back?" "You sure they allow that?" I asked.

16
00:05:20,512 --> 00:05:37,632
"My supervisor asked me to get his signed too." The supervisor was
standing behind a baggage cart pretending he hadn't sent the nigga
over. I pointed at him. He gave up the performance and came running
with his badge in his hand. Tank watched the little line form.

17
00:05:37,882 --> 00:06:02,848
"Nigga, you ain't even reached customs." "Customs reached me." "These
niggas got jobs." "They improving their workplaces." Rosa took a pen
out of her bag and handed it to Shawna. "Sign the pretty side. Niggas
gonna frame these." We signed the badges. The supervisor asked whether
he could name the terminal lounge after me. Rusk said that required
royal authorization.

18
00:06:03,098 --> 00:06:27,936
The supervisor looked from Rusk to the throne to me and appeared to
solve the question in a way the master of ceremonies didn't enjoy. "We
can put up a temporary sign," he said. "Nigga, that's initiative," I
told him. By the time Vesper reached us, a porter was carrying a
whiteboard across the terminal. Somebody had written CAPTAIN AIDEN'S
ARRIVAL LOUNGE in blue marker.

19
00:06:28,186 --> 00:06:52,314
Underneath, in smaller letters, the younger worker had added AND
SHAWNA'S. My wife saw it. "He gets a tip." "Nigga gets a promotion if
the king situation works out." Tank shook his head. "We been here
eleven minutes." "And you wasting them counting, my nigga. Look alive.
The country learning." "Lord whatever," I said. "Nigga, I'm tired. My
wife looks beautiful.

20
00:06:52,564 --> 00:07:12,116
My brother got a suit in that bag that cost more than your first
apartment. Look at that nigga. Does he look like he packed patience?"
Tank lifted the garment bag. "This my good suit. Don't make a nigga
meet you in it angry." "So show us our rooms," I told Rusk, "or bring
that throne closer.

21
00:07:12,366 --> 00:07:32,809
Nigga can keep talking while I enjoy my future furniture." Rusk's face
tightened. A few of the riflemen looked at each other. That little
look meant they had already realized the same thing I had: their boss
was standing too close to my hood. Then somebody started clapping.
Slow. Three times.

22
00:07:33,059 --> 00:07:49,366
A woman came down the airport steps in a dark green coat with nothing
timid about it. Black hair pinned high. A gold snake around one wrist.
Two guards carrying her luggage like they were transporting the last
clean water on earth.

23
00:07:49,616 --> 00:08:09,463
She was thirty-seven, I found out later, and she had the kind of face
that could make a man apologize for a crime she had committed.
"Aiden," she said. "That's usually who it is." "Queen Vesper Vane."
"Queen of what?" "You ask that before you kiss my hand?" "Nigga, I'm
married before I ask either." Shawna laughed.

24
00:08:09,713 --> 00:08:33,379
Vesper looked at her, then at the wedding ring, then back at me with a
smile that got sharper instead of smaller. "How unfortunate for the
city." "The city's gonna survive," Shawna said. "I'm less sure about
your master of ceremonies." Vesper turned one finger and the gold
rifles lowered. "Lord Rusk mistakes anticipation for authority. Your
rooms are ready.

25
00:08:33,629 --> 00:08:56,882
The opening procession is in forty minutes." "We just flew in." "The
kings wait for nobody." A jet engine started somewhere behind me. My
police badge shone in the sun. I was looking at a queen, a throne, a
thousand windows full of nosy rich people, and a city that thought
forty minutes was enough time to put my wife in a dress.

26
00:08:57,132 --> 00:09:21,194
"They finna learn," I said. At the hotel entrance, the porter
recognized me halfway through lifting my bag. "Oh, shit. You're—" The
handle slipped. The bag hit the marble. My shoe slid under Rusk, my
shirt landed on his foot, and our wedding photograph bounced face down
beside the luggage cart. "Nigga, catch my marriage!" Shawna and the
porter reached it together.

27
00:09:21,444 --> 00:09:44,691
She turned the frame over. Whole glass. Whole smile. Me looking at her
like somebody had finally given my eyes a useful assignment. "We're
still married," she said. "Good. Nigga, the shoe can file its own
complaint." The porter kept both hands under the frame after Shawna
had it. He was scared to let go. "Captain, I am so sorry. I watched
the race.

28
00:09:44,941 --> 00:10:06,861
The island. My brother said the wedding picture was fake." Shawna
looked at him. "Which part?" "He said nobody gets all that." "Your
brother sounds single," Rosa said. The second porter wheezed, tried to
turn it into a cough, and bent to recover my shoe. Rusk moved his foot
precisely far enough to make the nigga crawl another six inches.

29
00:10:07,111 --> 00:10:28,909
Tank put one finger against Rusk's shoulder and moved the entire lord.
"Nigga needs the shoe." "You might ask." "Nigga, I might carry you. We
exploring options." My wife finally eased the photograph out of the
first man's hands. "What's your name?" "Emil." "Emil, pick up the bag.
Breathe first." He breathed. Picked it up.

30
00:10:29,159 --> 00:10:50,325
The second porter tucked my shirt inside while Mercedes tried to slide
the recovered shoe onto my foot. "Other foot, nigga," Porsche told
her. "I'm giving a presentation." "You giving him two right feet. His
wife needs that nigga to dance." Shawna held out her hand. I took it
and gave her one slow turn on the marble.

31
00:10:50,575 --> 00:11:07,299
Emil forgot the bag again, but this time Tank caught its handle
without looking. "Nigga," Tank said, "you get one miracle per
driveway." Emil laughed hard enough to stop apologizing. That helped.
The next time he lifted the bag, he lifted a bag.

32
00:11:07,549 --> 00:11:30,465
My wife kept the photograph tucked against her instead of handing it
back, and I saw the little look he gave her for that. Relief.
Gratitude. Permission to finish one ordinary job after meeting a nigga
had briefly ruined his motor skills. Rusk pointed toward the doors.
"The procession begins in—" "Nigga, my shoe just got here," I told
him.

33
00:11:30,715 --> 00:11:56,832
"Let the whole delegation arrive." Our hotel had once been a palace.
You could tell because getting to the bathroom required crossing land
somebody had probably died over. Marble stairs, red carpets,
chandeliers thick as trees. Two young men tried to take Shawna's bags
and accidentally competed for the same handle until she assigned them
separate suitcases. Our suite overlooked the harbor.

34
00:11:57,082 --> 00:12:21,561
Modern yachts sat under stone walls older than everybody's grudges.
Ferraris crawled along the waterfront between flower stalls and armed
men drinking coffee. Above the city, on a black hill, Zero's palace
stood with every window shut against the afternoon. Shawna walked out
onto the balcony and let the sea wind move her hair. "That's pretty."
I looked at her instead.

35
00:12:21,811 --> 00:12:41,226
"Yeah." "You didn't even look." "I looked where I wanted." She turned
with that smile I had crossed whole cities to keep, and I caught her
around the waist before she could say something that would have had me
canceling the tournament. For a minute there were no kings. No
invitations. No bullet scars.

36
00:12:41,476 --> 00:13:03,665
Just my wife with her hands at my collar, straightening something that
hadn't been crooked until she decided it needed attention. "You gonna
behave tonight?" "You looking at the most beautiful behavior a nigga
ever brought overseas." "Aiden." "Nigga, you said my name like I
already did it." "You looked at the throne like you were measuring the
balcony." "That's planning.

37
00:13:03,915 --> 00:13:26,270
A nigga got a wife. He thinks about where she's gonna sit." "Beside
you when you behave." "Then I'm gonna misbehave beautifully enough you
stay close." She kissed me once, hard enough to make that answer
official. A knock came at the door. Tank carried in a black case with
the hotel crest on it. "Somebody sent you a welcome present." I opened
it.

38
00:13:26,520 --> 00:13:49,448
Inside was a pistol plated in white gold, a key to a red Ferrari, and
a note. FOR THE MAN WHO NEEDS HELP ARRIVING ON TIME. "Who sent it?"
"Vesper." Shawna read the note over my shoulder. "She better send me
something." Another knock. Rosa came through holding a long green box.
"That queen sent you emerald earrings," she told Shawna.

39
00:13:49,698 --> 00:14:12,465
"I was gonna steal them, but Tank looked disappointed before I even
did it." "I was looking at your shoes." "You were looking with
judgment." "Baby, one heel is a weapon." "Both of them are weapons.
Keep up." Shawna opened the earrings, admired them, and set them
beside the mirror without putting them on. She chose a blue pair I had
given her instead.

40
00:14:12,715 --> 00:14:36,202
Nigga, my whole chest went stupid. People kept trying to give me
cities, but my wife choosing my earrings could still knock the sense
out of me faster than any man alive. By the time we came downstairs,
the procession had started without us. There were drums outside.
Horns. Men on black horses. Women in gowns riding in open cars.

41
00:14:36,452 --> 00:14:57,408
Every balcony on the avenue had a banner hanging from it. We were
supposed to join at the front, behind the ceremonial carriage carrying
an empty cushion where the Crown of Midnight would eventually sit. The
Ferrari was waiting at the curb. So was a young hotel manager who
looked ready to start a new life somewhere else.

42
00:14:57,658 --> 00:15:14,551
"Captain Aiden, the avenue has been closed." "Open it." "I cannot. The
procession route is sealed." I looked at the route. I looked at the
Ferrari. I looked at the elevated tram line running down the middle of
the street. Tank saw me looking.

43
00:15:14,801 --> 00:15:39,273
"Nigga." "What?" "Nigga, that's a train track." "That's a road with
confidence." "For a train." "What this nigga have that I don't?"
"Tracks. A schedule. A whole different vehicle." "And I got my wife
looking at me. Nigga better keep his schedule." Shawna was already
getting into the passenger seat. "Don't scratch my side." Rosa grabbed
Tank's sleeve before he could climb in behind us.

44
00:15:39,523 --> 00:15:57,796
"We taking the normal road. I want to arrive with my hairstyle still
believing in God." I drove the Ferrari through the hotel courtyard,
past a fountain, up a service ramp, and onto the low platform where
the trams came through. A bell rang. People screamed.

45
00:15:58,046 --> 00:16:20,320
A tram driver leaned out and saw me coming toward him in a car that
cost enough to buy his entire argument. I took the outside rail. The
Ferrari tilted. Shawna held her hair with one hand and my thigh with
the other. "Aiden." "I got it." "I know. I'm saying your name because
I like it." Nigga, I almost missed the turn.

46
00:16:20,570 --> 00:16:41,101
We dropped from the platform into the procession between two marching
bands. One band stopped. The other started playing louder like they
were trying to survive through talent. My front tires landed inches
from a drummer's shoes. He looked at me, looked at the Ferrari, and
kept the beat. I threw him a stack of money.

47
00:16:41,351 --> 00:17:04,879
"That's professionalism, my nigga." The crowd recognized the badge
first. Then my face. Then the red car where no red car was supposed to
be. "Aiden!" Somebody yelled it from a balcony. Another voice caught
it. By the time we reached the empty royal carriage, the whole avenue
was saying my name. Shawna stood just enough in her seat to wave.

48
00:17:05,129 --> 00:17:28,144
Her blue dress caught the sun. Cameras turned away from kings who had
spent years preparing to be looked at and pointed at my wife arriving
late with me. A man in a purple limousine slammed his fist against his
window. "You have broken the order!" "Nigga, I improved it!" That was
when the first shot hit the ceremonial carriage. The empty cushion
jumped.

49
00:17:28,394 --> 00:17:54,559
A horse reared. The music tore apart into separate frightened noises.
I saw three black vans pull out from a side street. Men in white masks
stood through their roof openings. They weren't firing into the crowd.
Their guns tracked the cars carrying the visiting kings. One burst
shattered the purple limousine's windshield. Another took the mirror
off my Ferrari. Shawna dropped into her seat.

50
00:17:54,809 --> 00:18:16,985
"Now you can scratch my side." I hit the gas. The Ferrari crossed in
front of the carriage as the next burst came. Glass broke above us. I
pulled the white-gold pistol from its case and fired toward the
nearest masked man while Shawna grabbed a fallen parade banner and
threw it across the windshield of the van coming alongside.

51
00:18:17,235 --> 00:18:40,405
The driver saw nothing but the city's royal crest. He hit a flower
cart so hard roses filled the air like the street had exploded
romantically. "Baby, you wrapped that nigga's whole vehicle!" "You
like my throw?" "Nigga, I would marry that throw if I hadn't married
the woman!" "Then stop looking so pleased with that gun. Who gave you
that?" "Queen!

52
00:18:40,655 --> 00:19:01,932
Nigga, we can argue after the florist stops flying!" The second van
came at the carriage. Its driver wanted the road open and didn't care
how many horses had to disappear to make that happen. I cut between
them and caught his bumper with the Ferrari's back corner. The whole
car jolted. My shoulder slammed the seat.

53
00:19:02,182 --> 00:19:23,364
Blue heat sparked inside my arms, that thunder I could call for a
little while if I was willing to pay for it afterward. I didn't spend
it yet. A little power was good. Knowing when a nigga needed to keep
some was better. I drove up onto the broad stone steps of the opera
house. People scattered behind columns.

54
00:19:23,614 --> 00:19:39,633
The van followed until its front end struck a statue base and stopped
hard enough to throw the masked gunman against his own roof. The third
van turned toward the harbor. I went after it. "Seat belt," I said.
Shawna pulled it tight.

55
00:19:39,883 --> 00:20:02,191
"You say that every time we're already flying." "Because you listen
beautifully under pressure." We passed fish stalls, a wedding party,
and a priest who lifted his hands at exactly the right moment for our
car to miss his sleeves. The van cut onto a loading pier. A cargo
crane stood over the water with a steel container hanging from it.

56
00:20:02,441 --> 00:20:22,833
Beyond the pier, Vesper's black speedboat waited with its engines
running. The masked men were not trying to escape the city. They were
trying to reach her boat. I saw Vesper on the upper dock. She saw me
see her. Neither one of us smiled. The van braked beneath the crane.
Three men jumped out.

57
00:20:23,083 --> 00:20:45,824
One carried a narrow silver case that must have come from the carriage
during the confusion. The cushion had been empty. Something beneath it
hadn't been. I hit the blue thunder. For three seconds the whole world
became sharp. My hands, the wheel, the engine, the air in my teeth.
The Ferrari leaped forward with blue fire running across the hood.

58
00:20:46,074 --> 00:21:07,082
Shawna shouted my name and it sounded like a song somebody had turned
all the way up. We went off the end of the loading ramp. The car
struck the hanging container with its front wheels, rode the metal
side at an angle no mechanic on earth would have signed his name
under, and dropped onto the dock between the men and the boat.

59
00:21:07,332 --> 00:21:29,582
Every window on the pier shook when we landed. My arms went dead-
heavy. That was the price. I let the thunder go before it took more
than I had to spend. One masked man raised his weapon. Shawna opened
her door into him. The second slipped on the roses still caught
beneath our tire. I put him down before he could stand.

60
00:21:29,832 --> 00:21:48,018
The third held the silver case over the water. "Stop or I drop it!" I
got out slowly, my legs arguing about the landing. "Nigga, you keep
threatening me with stuff I don't know the price of." "It belongs to
the emperor!" "That explains why you're scared." He threw it.

61
00:21:48,268 --> 00:22:06,779
I caught the case against my chest with one hand and caught him by his
coat with the other. For a second we were both leaning out over the
harbor. He stared at the water. I stared at him. "Nigga, can you
swim?" "No!" "You stole a case, ran to the harbor, and dressed for a
fucking ballroom?

62
00:22:07,030 --> 00:22:30,052
Nigga, which part did you plan?" "Please!" "I'm holding you, my nigga.
That's why you still get to ask questions above water. Stop kicking my
car." I dragged him back and dropped him on the dock. Harbor police
were finally arriving, breathless, uniforms immaculate enough to prove
they'd missed most of the trouble. Their chief took one look at my
badge.

63
00:22:30,302 --> 00:22:47,683
"Captain Aiden?" "Arrest these niggas. And somebody get my wife a
different car. This one got opinions now." The chief saluted. Nigga,
he saluted so hard his hat nearly left him. Vesper came down the steps
without hurrying. Her guards stayed above.

64
00:22:47,934 --> 00:23:07,508
She looked at the destroyed Ferrari, the captured attackers, my wife
standing on the dock with one emerald box still in her handbag, and
the silver case in my hands. "You are very difficult to welcome." "You
sent the car." "I expected you to use the street." "You should have
said that." I opened the case.

65
00:23:07,757 --> 00:23:28,699
Inside lay a strip of black velvet and a heavy gold seal marked with a
crown. No jewels. No magic. Just an old piece of authority a whole lot
of men had nearly died trying to move from one place to another.
Vesper's eyes changed when she saw it. "The signet of invitation," she
said.

66
00:23:28,949 --> 00:23:50,459
"It admits one claimant to the private rounds." "I thought I was
already invited." "You were invited to watch." Shawna came beside me
and closed the case. "That's embarrassing for whoever sent the
invitation." By evening the city had put my face on the side of a
building. I hadn't asked. Nigga, I had been taking a shower.

67
00:23:50,709 --> 00:24:07,637
I came out in a towel and there I was outside our balcony, forty feet
tall, stepping out of the wrecked Ferrari with the silver case in my
hand. Underneath it, somebody had written THE KING FROM THE WEST. Tank
stood at the balcony rail with a drink.

68
00:24:07,887 --> 00:24:31,772
"Niggas got your good side." "I ain't got a bad one." "Your left
shoulder looks tired." "Nigga, that's history." "History needs ice."
"Then put ice on the real nigga. That nigga outside forty feet tall.
We can't afford his treatment." Tank looked from me to the building
and started laughing into his drink. Shawna sat at the vanity putting
on my blue earrings.

69
00:24:32,022 --> 00:24:50,390
Her dress for dinner was black, fitted, and personally disrespectful
to every other plan I had made that night. I went behind her and put
my hands on her shoulders. "We can stay in." "You just stole a king's
invitation." "I can steal dinner too." She looked at me in the mirror.

70
00:24:50,640 --> 00:25:12,893
"I want to see what they do when you walk in." So did I. Downstairs,
Lord Rusk waited by the throne from the airport. It had somehow
reached the hotel before our luggage. The silver cape was gone. His
new coat was black, and there was a bandage across one eyebrow where
the parade had given him a different opinion about the afternoon.

71
00:25:13,143 --> 00:25:37,459
"Captain," he said carefully. "The council has acknowledged your
claim." "Good." "There are rules." I sat down on the throne to adjust
my cuff. Every conversation in the lobby stopped. Shawna stood beside
me, her hand resting on my shoulder like she had been born knowing
where a crown would eventually fit. "Aight," I told Rusk. "Start with
the interesting ones."
